                      (        forth.asm):00001         * 6309 Forth based on my 1984/07/16 TRS-80 Model 1 level II ROM implementation.
                      (        forth.asm):00002         *
                      (        forth.asm):00003         * This work is dedicated to Alain Pinaud, author of "Programmer en Forth"
                      (        forth.asm):00004         * published by Editions du P.S.I. in 1983--i.e. my virtual mentor in the field.
                      (        forth.asm):00005         * Special thanks go William Astle for his fantastic LW Tools utility set and
                      (        forth.asm):00006         * to Robert Lipe for his advice on serial line handling. Apache subversion
                      (        forth.asm):00007         * and the sdiff utility also were on my side all the time.
                      (        forth.asm):00008         *
                      (        forth.asm):00009         * Also credited for their help: Justin Poirier (seminal HW design), Daniel
                      (        forth.asm):00010         * Tufvesson (original CompactFlash interface), Peter Minuth (general Forth
                      (        forth.asm):00011         * guruness), Paul E. Bennett (ANSI compatibility advice); Michel Jean, Bill
                      (        forth.asm):00012         * Ragsdale, Pablo Hugo Reda, Matthias Koch, Demitri Peynado and Bernd Paysan
                      (        forth.asm):00013         * for contributed application level code; Carsten Strotmann for most of the
                      (        forth.asm):00014         * benchmarking code (see https://theultimatebenchmark.org/); Gerry Jackson and
                      (        forth.asm):00015         * Steve R. Palmer (see https://github.com/gerryjackson/forth2012-test-suite)
                      (        forth.asm):00016         * for selected bits and pieces of the Forth2012 test suite
                      (        forth.asm):00017         * (see https://forth-standard.org/). Ruvim Pinka provided expertise on the
                      (        forth.asm):00018         * nitty-gritty details of a correct POSTPONE implementation.
                      (        forth.asm):00019         *
                      (        forth.asm):00020         * This is a native Forth. Not a threaded interpretive implementation.
                      (        forth.asm):00021         * Worth noticing is the fact that the return stack does not hold return
                      (        forth.asm):00022         * addresses at all. All what is stored there is loop indexes and input stream
                      (        forth.asm):00023         * parameters. Actual return addresses are kept in the system stack. All in all,
                      (        forth.asm):00024         * this is the result of the work of a 19 year old, heavily revisited 35 years
                      (        forth.asm):00025         * later. The downside of this implementation is that the generated code is
                      (        forth.asm):00026         * about 30% larger than a threaded interpretive implementation would be.
                      (        forth.asm):00027         * So it goes...
                      (        forth.asm):00028         *
                      (        forth.asm):00029         * Control flow constructs have been re-implemented based on Wonyong Koh's
                      (        forth.asm):00030         * hForth for the 8086. The original code can be consulted at
                      (        forth.asm):00031         * https://github.com/nealcrook/hForth. Of particular interest is
                      (        forth.asm):00032         * 8086/HF86RAM.ASM. Entries on the control flow stack (implemented on a
                      (        forth.asm):00033         * dedicated stack) are two cell entities that consist of a parameter
                      (        forth.asm):00034         * (an address), on the top of which a tag identifying the type of address
                      (        forth.asm):00035         * is pushed. They are:
                      (        forth.asm):00036         *
                      (        forth.asm):00037         * Control-flow stack item    Representation (parameter and type)
                      (        forth.asm):00038         * -----------------------    -------------------------------------
                      (        forth.asm):00039         * dest                       control-flow destination      0
                      (        forth.asm):00040         * orig                       control-flow origin           1
                      (        forth.asm):00041         * of-sys                     OF origin                     2 [1]
                      (        forth.asm):00042         * case-sys                   x (any value)                 3 [1]
                      (        forth.asm):00043         * do-sys                     ?DO origin                    DO destination
                      (        forth.asm):00044         * colon-sys                  xt of current definition     -1 [1]
                      (        forth.asm):00045         *
                      (        forth.asm):00046         * [1] Not implemented in Z79Forth/A.
                      (        forth.asm):00047         * 
                      (        forth.asm):00048         * This mechanism allows for verification of balanced control flow constructs.
                      (        forth.asm):00049         *
                      (        forth.asm):00050         * The code generated is limited to a very small instruction set:
                      (        forth.asm):00051         *
                      (        forth.asm):00052         * LDXOPC        $8E     LDX (immediate)
                      (        forth.asm):00053         * JMPOPC        $7E     JMP (extended)
                      (        forth.asm):00054         * JSROPC        $BD     JSR (extended)
                      (        forth.asm):00055         * RTSOPC        $39     RTS (inherent)
                      (        forth.asm):00056         * BCSOPC        $2503   BCS *+5 (relative) Used in LOOP, +LOOP
                      (        forth.asm):00057         * BNEOPC        $2603   BNE *+5 (relative) Used in ?DO, IF, UNTIL
                      (        forth.asm):00058         *
                      (        forth.asm):00059         * On error (uncaught exception), all stacks will be cleared, BASE will be set to
                      (        forth.asm):00060         * decimal and the system stack pointer (Sreg) will be reset.
                      (        forth.asm):00061         * ABORT ABORT" and QUIT enforce their own ANS94 standard behaviour.
                      (        forth.asm):00062         *
                      (        forth.asm):00063         * RESTRICT is non-standard. It comes from GNU Forth (VolksForth). The " OK"
                      (        forth.asm):00064         * non-prompt string also does, by the way. Thanks to Anton Ertl for his terse
                      (        forth.asm):00065         * yet valuable input.
                      (        forth.asm):00066         *
                      (        forth.asm):00067         * .' (dot-tick) is non-standard. It comes from SwiftForth. It will be supported
                      (        forth.asm):00068         * whether or not the symbolic stack dump has been configured (see SSDFEAT in
                      (        forth.asm):00069         * constants.asm). However, please note that effective symbolic references will
                      (        forth.asm):00070         * be resolved only if the feature was enabled at compilation time. Otherwise
                      (        forth.asm):00071         * a simple HEX print of the cell at the top of the data stack will be
                      (        forth.asm):00072         * performed. This is meant to support Forth source code that does not depend
                      (        forth.asm):00073         * on the feature vector (see examples/dis.4th).
                      (        forth.asm):00074         *
                      (        forth.asm):00075         * MONITOR and ICHECK are also non-standard. They are intended to maintain and
                      (        forth.asm):00076         * verify the integrity of a checksum of the code section of RAM resident
                      (        forth.asm):00077         * words, with the exception of VARIABLEs and CREATEd words. CREATEd words,
                      (        forth.asm):00078         * if subject to the MONITOR treatment will also carry a code section
                      (        forth.asm):00079         * checksum, although this is not the default behaviour. The checksum will
                      (        forth.asm):00080         * consist in an extra byte added to every word's header. MONITOR and ICHECK
                      (        forth.asm):00081         * will be available whether or not the reliability feature has been configured
                      (        forth.asm):00082         * (see RELFEAT in constants.asm). They will only carry effective semantics
                      (        forth.asm):00083         * if the feature was actually enabled at compilation time. This is meant to
                      (        forth.asm):00084         * support Forth source code that does not depend on the feature vector.
                      (        forth.asm):00085         *
                      (        forth.asm):00086         * Experimental MC146818 RTC support: the feature is disabled by default
                      (        forth.asm):00087         * (see RTCFEAT in constants.asm) because it relies on undocumented schematics.
                      (        forth.asm):00088         * Also, the required underlying circuitry is not intended to ever become an
                      (        forth.asm):00089         * integral part of the Z79Forth reference board itself. Some better designed
                      (        forth.asm):00090         * form of it might eventually surface in the form of an extension specification.
                      (        forth.asm):00091         * At the time of this writing this is just a proof of concept, but whether or
                      (        forth.asm):00092         * not the feature is enabled, three extra words will be added to the dictionary.
                      (        forth.asm):00093         * They are RTC@ RTC! and TICKS They can be safely ignored.
                      (        forth.asm):00094         *
                      (        forth.asm):00095         * Forth source code portability note:
                      (        forth.asm):00096         * Because Z79Forth does not use the return stack to store return addresses,
                      (        forth.asm):00097         * it makes it quite easy to write code that is not readily portable to classic
                      (        forth.asm):00098         * threaded interpretive implementations. The resulting code will be simpler but
                      (        forth.asm):00099         * portability will be limited.
                      (        forth.asm):00100         *
                      (        forth.asm):00101         * Miscellaneous notes: RA stands for return address; EP for entry point.
                      (        forth.asm):00102         * CF is a shortcut for CompactFlash. TOS means top of the data/normal stack.
                      (        forth.asm):00103         * Occasionally, CFA is used for code field address which, in this
                      (        forth.asm):00104         * implementation, is a synonym for compilation address. XT means execution
                      (        forth.asm):00105         * token--the ANSI term for a compilation address. MSC stands for most
                      (        forth.asm):00106         * significant cell; LSC for least significant cell.
                      (        forth.asm):00107         *
                      (        forth.asm):00108         * The complete guide to the HD6309 extended instruction set can be found at:
                      (        forth.asm):00109         * https://cyberabi.ipower.com/Downloads/The_6309_Book.pdf. For convenience,
                      (        forth.asm):00110         * and with the author's explicit agreement, this document has been included
                      (        forth.asm):00111         * in this distribution. This is recommended reading for anyone altering this
                      (        forth.asm):00112         * code or trying to make some sense of it!!!
                      (        forth.asm):00113         *
                      (        forth.asm):00114         * This whole effort started out as a porting endeavour and ended up being a
                      (        forth.asm):00115         * substantial rewrite, trying to take advantage of the features of the 6309
                      (        forth.asm):00116         * as much as possible. The primary goals of this implementation are:
                      (        forth.asm):00117         * reliability, performance and code compactness. A number of bugs in the
                      (        forth.asm):00118         * original code have been fixed--some remain for sure!
                      (        forth.asm):00119         *
                      (        forth.asm):00120         * Obligatory literary reference:
                      (        forth.asm):00121         * "The paper is very heavy going, and I should never have read it, had I not
                      (        forth.asm):00122         * written it myself." John E. Littlewood (1885-1977).
                      (        forth.asm):00123         *
                      (        forth.asm):00124         * The original soundtrack for this work is available at:
                      (        forth.asm):00125         * https://youtu.be/YqXZtGyFyDo?t=4023 (J.S. Bach BWV 1080, contrapunctus 14).
                      (        forth.asm):00126         
0000                  (        forth.asm):00127         pragma  opt cd,operandsizewarning
                      (        forth.asm):00128         
                      (        forth.asm):00129                 include constants.asm
                      (    constants.asm):00001         * Begin tunable parameters section.
                      (    constants.asm):00002         
     0000             (    constants.asm):00003         CSSNTVE equ     0               Words and HEX numbers are case sensitive if NZ
     0001             (    constants.asm):00004         SSDFEAT equ     1               Symbolic stack dump is enabled by default
     0001             (    constants.asm):00005         RELFEAT set     1               Set to 1 to enable the reliability feature
     0000             (    constants.asm):00006         MCCFEAT equ     0               McCabe cyclomatic complexity evaluator
                      (    constants.asm):00007         *                               Exception support require this to be disabled
     0000             (    constants.asm):00008         RTCFEAT equ     0               Cool but the reliability feature must go...
     0001             (    constants.asm):00009         TCRFEAT equ     1               Tail call removal feature is enabled by default
                      (    constants.asm):00010         
     0000             (    constants.asm):00011         DEBUG   set     0               Enforce assertions and miscellaneous checks
     0001             (    constants.asm):00012         HVNMI   equ     1               NMI handler support
     0000             (    constants.asm):00013         HVNMI2  equ     0               NMI handler support (async input debugging)
                      (    constants.asm):00014         * Loop count for MS. This is busy waiting, so we depend on the CPU clock speed.
     031A             (    constants.asm):00015         MSLCNT  equ     794             at 4 MHz native mode
                      (    constants.asm):00016         *MSLCNT equ     994             at 5 MHz native mode
                      (    constants.asm):00017         
                      (    constants.asm):00018         * End tunable parameters section.
                      (    constants.asm):00019         
                      (    constants.asm):00020                 IFNE    RTCFEAT
0000                  (    constants.asm):00021         RELFEAT set     0               RTCFEAT disables RELFEAT
                      (    constants.asm):00022                 ELSE
                      (    constants.asm):00023                 IFNE    HVNMI
                      (    constants.asm):00024                 IFNE    HVNMI2
0000                  (    constants.asm):00025         RELFEAT set     0               (HVNMI and HVNMI2) disable RELFEAT
                      (    constants.asm):00026                 ENDC                    HVNMI2
                      (    constants.asm):00027                 ENDC                    HVNMI
                      (    constants.asm):00028                 ENDC                    RTCFEAT
                      (    constants.asm):00029         
                      (    constants.asm):00030         * Intrinsic ANS94 support prevents both DEBUG and the reliability feature.
     0000             (    constants.asm):00031         RELFEAT set     0
     0000             (    constants.asm):00032         DEBUG   set     0
                      (    constants.asm):00033         
                      (    constants.asm):00034         * Memory map.
     0000             (    constants.asm):00035         RAMSTRT equ     $0000
     8000             (    constants.asm):00036         RAMSIZE equ     $8000
     C000             (    constants.asm):00037         IOSTRT  equ     $C000
     E000             (    constants.asm):00038         ROMSTRT equ     $E000
     FFF0             (    constants.asm):00039         VECTBL  equ     $FFF0
                      (    constants.asm):00040         
                      (    constants.asm):00041         * Base address for global variables (direct page addressed).
     0100             (    constants.asm):00042         VARSPC  equ     (RAMSTRT+$100)
                      (    constants.asm):00043         
                      (    constants.asm):00044         * The 74HCT138 (U7) IO address decoder maps one 1 KB area per usable device.
     C000             (    constants.asm):00045         DEV0    equ     $C000           Compact Flash memory module (optional)
     C400             (    constants.asm):00046         DEV1    equ     $C400
     C800             (    constants.asm):00047         DEV2    equ     $C800
     CC00             (    constants.asm):00048         DEV3    equ     $CC00
     D000             (    constants.asm):00049         DEV4    equ     $D000
     D400             (    constants.asm):00050         DEV5    equ     $D400           MC146818 RTC (optional)
     D800             (    constants.asm):00051         DEV6    equ     $D800           HD63B50 unit 0
     DC00             (    constants.asm):00052         DEV7    equ     $DC00
                      (    constants.asm):00053         
     D800             (    constants.asm):00054         ACIACTL equ     DEV6
     D801             (    constants.asm):00055         ACIADAT equ     DEV6+1
                      (    constants.asm):00056         
                      (    constants.asm):00057         * ACIA control register bits.
     0003             (    constants.asm):00058         ACRST   equ     %00000011       ACIA master reset
                      (    constants.asm):00059         
                      (    constants.asm):00060         * 1.84320 MHz Y1: 115200 bps in the direct path, 38400 bps in the DIV3 path
     0001             (    constants.asm):00061         ACDIV16 equ     %00000001       ACIA div 16
                      (    constants.asm):00062         
     0014             (    constants.asm):00063         AC8N1   equ     %00010100       ACIA 8N1
     0000             (    constants.asm):00064         ACRTS0  equ     %00000000       ACIA RTS# low
     0040             (    constants.asm):00065         ACRTS1  equ     %01000000       ACIA RTS# high
     0080             (    constants.asm):00066         ACRDINT equ     %10000000       IRQ on RDRF
                      (    constants.asm):00067         
     0043             (    constants.asm):00068         ACIRSET equ     ACRTS1|ACRST
     00D5             (    constants.asm):00069         ACIRTS1 equ     ACRTS1|ACRDINT|AC8N1|ACDIV16
     0095             (    constants.asm):00070         ACIRTS0 equ     ACRTS0|ACRDINT|AC8N1|ACDIV16
                      (    constants.asm):00071         
                      (    constants.asm):00072         * ACIA status register bits.
     0001             (    constants.asm):00073         ACIRDRF equ     %00000001       Receive data register full
     0002             (    constants.asm):00074         ACITDRE equ     %00000010       Transmit data register empty
     0020             (    constants.asm):00075         ACIOVRN equ     %00100000       Overrun status register bit
     0080             (    constants.asm):00076         ACIISVC equ     %10000000       Interrupt needs servicing
                      (    constants.asm):00077         
                      (    constants.asm):00078         * Compact Flash parameters.
     C000             (    constants.asm):00079         CFBASE  equ     DEV0
     C000             (    constants.asm):00080         CFDATAR equ     CFBASE          R/W data register
     C001             (    constants.asm):00081         CFERROR equ     CFBASE+1        RO error register
     C001             (    constants.asm):00082         CFFEATR equ     CFBASE+1        WO features register
     C002             (    constants.asm):00083         CFSCNTR equ     CFBASE+2        R/W sector count register
     C003             (    constants.asm):00084         CFSNUMR equ     CFBASE+3        R/W sector number register
     C004             (    constants.asm):00085         CFCLOWR equ     CFBASE+4        R/W cylinder low register
     C005             (    constants.asm):00086         CFCHIGR equ     CFBASE+5        R/W cylinder high register
     C006             (    constants.asm):00087         CFDRHDR equ     CFBASE+6        R/W drive/head register
     C007             (    constants.asm):00088         CFSTATR equ     CFBASE+7        RO status register
     C007             (    constants.asm):00089         CFCOMDR equ     CFBASE+7        WO command register
                      (    constants.asm):00090         
                      (    constants.asm):00091         * CF status bits.
     0080             (    constants.asm):00092         CFBSYB  equ     %10000000       BSY status bit
     0040             (    constants.asm):00093         CFRDYB  equ     %01000000       RDY status bit
     0020             (    constants.asm):00094         CFDWFB  equ     %00100000       DWF status bit (not used)
     0010             (    constants.asm):00095         CFDSCB  equ     %00010000       DSC status bit (not used)
     0008             (    constants.asm):00096         CFDRQB  equ     %00001000       DRQ status bit
     0001             (    constants.asm):00097         CFERRB  equ     %00000001       ERR status bit
                      (    constants.asm):00098         
     0200             (    constants.asm):00099         CFSCSZ  equ     $200            Compact Flash (IDE) sector size
                      (    constants.asm):00100         
                      (    constants.asm):00101         * CF commands.
     00EC             (    constants.asm):00102         CFIDDEV equ     $EC             Identify Device
     00EF             (    constants.asm):00103         CFSETFT equ     $EF             Set Feature
     0020             (    constants.asm):00104         CFRSCTS equ     $20             Read Sectors
     0030             (    constants.asm):00105         CFWSCTS equ     $30             Write Sectors
                      (    constants.asm):00106         
                      (    constants.asm):00107         * Buffer in-memory structure:
                      (    constants.asm):00108         * data: 1024 bytes.
                      (    constants.asm):00109         * term: Deprecated: 1 byte set to 0.
                      (    constants.asm):00110         * flags: 1 byte.
                      (    constants.asm):00111         * blknum: 2 bytes.
     0001             (    constants.asm):00112         BINUSE  equ     1               Buffer is allocated (the blknum field is valid)
     0002             (    constants.asm):00113         BMAPPD  equ     2               Block has been read from the CF device
     0004             (    constants.asm):00114         BDIRTY  equ     4               Block has been marked for update
     0400             (    constants.asm):00115         BLKSIZ  equ     2*CFSCSZ        Block size is 2 CF sectors (1 KB)
                      (    constants.asm):00116         * Buffer field offsets.
                      (    constants.asm):00117         * BOTERM is deprecated in the ANS94 implementation.
                      (    constants.asm):00118         *BOTERM equ     BLKSIZ          Base buffer to the 'term' field offset
     0401             (    constants.asm):00119         BOFLAGS equ     BLKSIZ+1        Base buffer to the 'flags' field offset
     0402             (    constants.asm):00120         BOBLKNO equ     BLKSIZ+2        Base buffer to the 'blknum' field offset
                      (    constants.asm):00121         
     0410             (    constants.asm):00122         BFDISP  equ     BUF1-BUF0       Offset between resident buffers
                      (    constants.asm):00123         
                      (    constants.asm):00124                 IFNE    RTCFEAT
                      (    constants.asm):00125         * MC146818 RTC registers.
0000                  (    constants.asm):00126         RTAS    equ     DEV5            Latch target register address offset
0000                  (    constants.asm):00127         RTDS    equ     (DEV5+1)        Actual target register access
                      (    constants.asm):00128         * RTC internal register offsets.
0000                  (    constants.asm):00129         RTOSEC  equ     0               Seconds
0000                  (    constants.asm):00130         RTOSECA equ     1               Seconds alarm
0000                  (    constants.asm):00131         RTOMIN  equ     2               Minutes
0000                  (    constants.asm):00132         RTOMINA equ     3               Minutes alarm
0000                  (    constants.asm):00133         RTOHOUR equ     4               Hours
0000                  (    constants.asm):00134         RTOHRA  equ     5               Hours alarm
0000                  (    constants.asm):00135         RTODOW  equ     6               Day of week
0000                  (    constants.asm):00136         RTODOM  equ     7               Day of month
0000                  (    constants.asm):00137         RTOMON  equ     8               Month
0000                  (    constants.asm):00138         RTOYEAR equ     9               Year
0000                  (    constants.asm):00139         RTOREGA equ     10              Register A
0000                  (    constants.asm):00140         RTOREGB equ     11              Register B
0000                  (    constants.asm):00141         RTOREGC equ     12              Register C
0000                  (    constants.asm):00142         RTOREGD equ     13              Register D
0000                  (    constants.asm):00143         RTOUMB  equ     14              Base of user defined NVRAM storage
0000                  (    constants.asm):00144         RTUMSZ  equ     50              Size of user defined NVRAM storage
0000                  (    constants.asm):00145         RTOPRES equ     (RTOUMB+RTUMSZ-1) RTC NVRAM offset for dectecting dev presence
                      (    constants.asm):00146         
                      (    constants.asm):00147         * Register A bits.
0000                  (    constants.asm):00148         RTAUIP  equ     $80             Update in progress
0000                  (    constants.asm):00149         RTADVRS equ     $70             Divider reset, not in operation
0000                  (    constants.asm):00150         RTADV32 equ     $20             In operation, 32 KHz time base
0000                  (    constants.asm):00151         RTARS64 equ     $A              32 KHz time base, 64 Hz PI (every 15.625 ms)
                      (    constants.asm):00152         
                      (    constants.asm):00153         * Register B bits.
0000                  (    constants.asm):00154         RTBSET  equ     $80
0000                  (    constants.asm):00155         RTBPIE  equ     $40
0000                  (    constants.asm):00156         RTBDM   equ     4               Set to 1 for binary register contents
0000                  (    constants.asm):00157         RTB24   equ     2               Set to 1 for 24 hour format
                      (    constants.asm):00158         
                      (    constants.asm):00159         * Register C bits.
0000                  (    constants.asm):00160         RTCPF   equ     $40             Periodic interrupt pending flag
                      (    constants.asm):00161                 ENDC                    RTCFEAT
                      (    constants.asm):00162         
                      (    constants.asm):00163         * ASCII trivia.
     0000             (    constants.asm):00164         NUL     equ     0               End of string marker
     0003             (    constants.asm):00165         ETX     equ     3               Control-C (intr)
     0008             (    constants.asm):00166         BS      equ     8               Backspace
     0009             (    constants.asm):00167         HT      equ     9               Horizontal tab
     000A             (    constants.asm):00168         LF      equ     $0A             Aka new line
     000D             (    constants.asm):00169         CR      equ     $0D             Carriage return
     0015             (    constants.asm):00170         NAK     equ     $15             Control-U (kill)
     0020             (    constants.asm):00171         SP      equ     $20             Aka BL in Forth
     0013             (    constants.asm):00172         XOFF    equ     $13             Aka DC3
     0011             (    constants.asm):00173         XON     equ     $11             Aka DC1
                      (    constants.asm):00174         
                      (    constants.asm):00175         * Stack sizes.
     0100             (    constants.asm):00176         NSTKSZ  equ     256             Expressed in bytes. Now only limited by RAM size
     0100             (    constants.asm):00177         RSTKSZ  equ     256             Expressed in bytes. Up to 64 nested loops
     0080             (    constants.asm):00178         CSTKSZ  equ     128             Expressed in bytes. Up to 32 double cells
     0030             (    constants.asm):00179         ESTKSZ  equ     (8*6)           Expressed in bytes. 8 exception frames.
                      (    constants.asm):00180         
                      (    constants.asm):00181         * Buffer sizes.
     0084             (    constants.asm):00182         CMDBFSZ equ     132             Command line entry buffer
     0050             (    constants.asm):00183         HEXBFSZ equ     80
     0048             (    constants.asm):00184         TBUFSZ  equ     72              Used by VLIST to print word name and CVNSTR
     0054             (    constants.asm):00185         PADBSZ  equ     84              79-STANDARD mandates a minimum of 64 bytes
     0040             (    constants.asm):00186         SERBSZ  equ     64              Serial buffer size. Needs to be a power of 2
                      (    constants.asm):00187         
                      (    constants.asm):00188         * Dictionary flag masks.
     0080             (    constants.asm):00189         IMDFLM  equ     $80             Immediate flag mask
     0040             (    constants.asm):00190         DEFFLM  equ     $40             Compilation only flag mask
                      (    constants.asm):00191                 IFNE    RELFEAT
0000                  (    constants.asm):00192         MONFLM  equ     $20             Monitored flag mask. This indicates that the
                      (    constants.asm):00193         *                               word to which it relates might be checked for
                      (    constants.asm):00194         *                               integrity. This applies by default to all words
                      (    constants.asm):00195         *                               defined with : and all constants. It might
                      (    constants.asm):00196         *                               also apply to any other CREATEd object by
                      (    constants.asm):00197         *                               resorting to the MONITOR word. Using MONITOR
                      (    constants.asm):00198         *                               on variable word contents is guaranteed to
                      (    constants.asm):00199         *                               raise ICHECK's attention.
                      (    constants.asm):00200                 ENDC
                      (    constants.asm):00201         
                      (    constants.asm):00202         * Division function codes and options.
     0000             (    constants.asm):00203         DVFSLMD equ     0               Function is /MOD
     0001             (    constants.asm):00204         DVFMOD  equ     1               Function is MOD
     0002             (    constants.asm):00205         DVFDIV  equ     2               Function is /
     0008             (    constants.asm):00206         DVOA1D  equ     8               Argument 1 is a double (FM/MOD SM/REM)
     0010             (    constants.asm):00207         DVOWSYM equ     16              Want symmetric division (default is floored)
     0007             (    constants.asm):00208         DVFMASK equ     7               Mask for extracting function codes
                      (    constants.asm):00209         
     001F             (    constants.asm):00210         WRLNMSK equ     $1F             31 character is the maximum word length
                      (    constants.asm):00211         
                      (    constants.asm):00212         * 6309 opcodes.
     008E             (    constants.asm):00213         LDXOPC  equ     $8E             LDX (immediate)
     007E             (    constants.asm):00214         JMPOPC  equ     $7E             JMP (extended)
     00BD             (    constants.asm):00215         JSROPC  equ     $BD             JSR (extended)
     0039             (    constants.asm):00216         RTSOPC  equ     $39             RTS (inherent)
     2503             (    constants.asm):00217         BCSOPC  equ     $2503           BCS *+5 (relative)
     2603             (    constants.asm):00218         BNEOPC  equ     $2603           BNE *+5 (relative)
     00C7             (    constants.asm):00219         ILLOPC  equ     $C7             An illegal operation code. Meant to raise a trap
                      (    constants.asm):00220         
     0001             (    constants.asm):00221         CFLAG   equ     1               CC bit 0 (C)
     0004             (    constants.asm):00222         ZFLAG   equ     4               CC bit 2 (Z)
     0010             (    constants.asm):00223         IFLAG   equ     $10             CC bit 4 (I)
     0040             (    constants.asm):00224         FFLAG   equ     $40             CC bit 6 (F)
                      (    constants.asm):00225         
                      (    constants.asm):00226         * RAM based execution token for @.
     0E34             (    constants.asm):00227         RAMFTCH set     WDICSPC+4       Dictionary header overhead is word's length + 3
                      (    constants.asm):00228                 IFNE    RELFEAT         The reliability features adds one byte to the
0000                  (    constants.asm):00229         RAMFTCH set     WDICSPC+5       header: a checksum.
                      (    constants.asm):00230                 ENDC
                      (    constants.asm):00231         
                      (    constants.asm):00232         * Error condition codes passed through Breg to SYSTHR8.
     FFFF             (    constants.asm):00233         EABORT  equ     -1      STD -- ABORT
     FFFE             (    constants.asm):00234         EABRTQ  equ     -2      STD -- ABORT"
     FFFD             (    constants.asm):00235         EDSOVF  equ     -3      STD -- DS overflow
     FFFC             (    constants.asm):00236         EDSUDF  equ     -4      STD -- DS underflow
     FFFB             (    constants.asm):00237         ERSOVF  equ     -5      STD -- RS overflow
     FFFA             (    constants.asm):00238         ERSUDF  equ     -6      STD -- RS underflow
     FFF7             (    constants.asm):00239         ESSEGV  equ     -9      STD -- Illegal argument (CHAR FIND PICK EXECUTE)
     FFF6             (    constants.asm):00240         EDIVZR  equ     -10     STD -- Division by zero (TRAP)
     FFF5             (    constants.asm):00241         EOORNG  equ     -11     STD -- OoR error
     FFF3             (    constants.asm):00242         EUNDEF  equ     -13     STD -- ? / Undefined word
     FFF2             (    constants.asm):00243         ESTATE  equ     -14     STD -- Incorrect STATE
     FFF0             (    constants.asm):00244         ENONAM  equ     -16     STD -- Missing word (POSTPONE : CREATE)
     FFED             (    constants.asm):00245         ENAMLN  equ     -19     STD -- Name too long
     FFEC             (    constants.asm):00246         ERONLY  equ     -20     STD -- RO word
     FFEB             (    constants.asm):00247         ENOSUP  equ     -21     STD -- IO error or TRAP (ILOP)
     FFEA             (    constants.asm):00248         EILCST  equ     -22     STD -- Illegal construct
     FFE4             (    constants.asm):00249         EUINTR  equ     -28     STD -- SIGINT
     FFE1             (    constants.asm):00250         ENOCRE  equ     -31     STD -- Not CREATEd
                      (    constants.asm):00251         * Allocated against the standard specification. These are not catchable--i.e.
                      (    constants.asm):00252         * we branch directly to ERRHDLR (under the 16 bit interface). They're not
                      (    constants.asm):00253         * recoverable anyway.
     FFE0             (    constants.asm):00254         EINOOR  equ     -32     >IN OoR
     FFDF             (    constants.asm):00255         EESOVF  equ     -33     ES overflow
                      (    constants.asm):00256         
                      (        forth.asm):00130         
                      (        forth.asm):00131         * Unchecked NPUSH. This is for situations in which there is absolutely no
                      (        forth.asm):00132         * chance of overflow. For instance, in case we just popped 2 cells and push
                      (        forth.asm):00133         * back one or two.
0000                  (        forth.asm):00134         UCNPUSH MACRO   NOEXPAND
                      (        forth.asm):00135                 pshu    x
                      (        forth.asm):00136                 ENDM
                      (        forth.asm):00137         
                      (        forth.asm):00138         * Unchecked NPOP. To be used only after trusted words have been invoked, i.e.
                      (        forth.asm):00139         * when one is positively sure that the data stack contains at least one cell.
0000                  (        forth.asm):00140         UCNPOP  MACRO   NOEXPAND
                      (        forth.asm):00141                 pulu    x
                      (        forth.asm):00142                 ENDM
                      (        forth.asm):00143         
                      (        forth.asm):00144         * Make sure minimum data stack requirements are satisfied upon word entry.
                      (        forth.asm):00145         * The requirement is expressed in cell size--2 bytes on the 6309.
                      (        forth.asm):00146         * \1 specifies the required number of cells.
0000                  (        forth.asm):00147         MINDREQ MACRO   NOEXPAND
                      (        forth.asm):00148                 ldd     #NSTBOT-(\1*2)  Cell count one expects to be stacked up
                      (        forth.asm):00149                 bra     CHKNDPT         No return if the condition is not met
                      (        forth.asm):00150                 ENDM
                      (        forth.asm):00151         
                      (        forth.asm):00152         * Reliability feature support: execution tokens.
                      (        forth.asm):00153         * \1 has the opcode we want to emit.
                      (        forth.asm):00154         * \2 has the execution token address, as if the header overhead always
                      (        forth.asm):00155         * was 3 bytes.
0000                  (        forth.asm):00156         RFXT    MACRO   NOEXPAND
                      (        forth.asm):00157                 IFNE    RELFEAT
                      (        forth.asm):00158                 \1      \2+1
                      (        forth.asm):00159                 ELSE
                      (        forth.asm):00160                 \1      \2
                      (        forth.asm):00161                 ENDC                    RELFEAT
                      (        forth.asm):00162                 ENDM
                      (        forth.asm):00163         
                      (        forth.asm):00164         * Reliability feature support: variable word header contents.
                      (        forth.asm):00165         * This is a dummy checksum only used for EEPROM resident words.
                      (        forth.asm):00166         * Those never are checked for code integrity by MONITOR.
0000                  (        forth.asm):00167         RFCS    MACRO   NOEXPAND
                      (        forth.asm):00168                 IFNE    RELFEAT
                      (        forth.asm):00169                 fcb     ILLOPC          Illegal opcode
                      (        forth.asm):00170                 ENDC                    RELFEAT
                      (        forth.asm):00171                 ENDM
                      (        forth.asm):00172         
                      (        forth.asm):00173         *******************************************************************************
                      (        forth.asm):00174         * RAM definitions. We cannot initialize globals from the assembly defs.
                      (        forth.asm):00175         * All we can do here is define addresses and size things up.
                      (        forth.asm):00176         
                      (        forth.asm):00177         * RAMSTRT is 0. We leave page 0 unused as a bug proof area.
                      (        forth.asm):00178         * When compiled in debug mode, this area is filled with illegal
                      (        forth.asm):00179         * instruction opcodes ($C7).
                      (        forth.asm):00180         
                      (        forth.asm):00181                 org     VARSPC
